# Secrets. `.env` itself stays tracked: it holds only VITE_SUPABASE_URL and the
# Supabase anon key, which are public by design (RLS is what protects the data)
# and are compiled into the client bundle anyway. Anything genuinely secret —
# the service-role key, the SMS gateway key — must go in a Vercel environment
# variable or a Supabase Edge Function secret, never in a committed file.
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production
.env.development.local

